# Deep-learning stack. On Windows/macOS PyPI wheels are CPU-only; on Linux (Colab/Kaggle) they are CUDA builds.
# On Colab/Kaggle prefer the image's preinstalled torch (see README "Colab/Kaggle"); versions are recorded per run.
# torchaudio is deliberately NOT used (DEC-14): its latest release (2.11.0) lags torch (2.14.x) and its wheels are
# ABI-tied to torch. Audio I/O = soundfile, resampling = soxr (via librosa), LFCC = torch.stft.
